Description: A click on the highlighted menu item chooses it
 In a menu, the first click on an item highlights it (as before) and a click
 on the item that is already highlighted works like Enter on the OK button.
 So a double-click runs a menu item, as on a desktop.
Author: Kilobyte <https://github.com/jgm240/kilobyte>

--- a/menubox.c
+++ b/menubox.c
@@ -554,6 +554,16 @@
 		key -= DLGK_MOUSE(KEY_MAX);
 		i = RowToItem(key);
 		if (i < max_choice) {
+		    /*
+		     * Kilobyte: clicking the item that is already highlighted
+		     * chooses it, so a double-click works like Enter on OK.
+		     */
+		    if (i == choice) {
+			button = 0;
+			dlg_draw_buttons(dialog, height - 2, 0, buttons, button, FALSE, width);
+			ungetch('\n');
+			continue;
+		    }
 		    found = TRUE;
 		} else {
 		    beep();
